# One person, two accounts. The repository is MochiNek0's, so that identity is
# the canonical one and the other maps onto it.
#
# This is here for a reason beyond a tidy `git shortlog`. The app is AGPL-3.0
# (see LICENSE), and a relicence is only the copyright holders' to make -- so
# "every commit in this history is by one person" is a claim someone may need
# to check, and a log that appears to list two contributors is the thing that
# would make them doubt it. Mapped by email alone, so it holds for commits
# under either display name.
#
# `GitHub <noreply@github.com>` is deliberately not mapped: it is the committer
# on merges made through the web UI, not an author, and rewriting it would
# hide who actually pressed the button.

MochiNek0 <mochinekoiiiiii@gmail.com> <bill.zhu@vibe.us>
